Not sure I understand your issue. Clustering per se does not affect the required buffer width. The question is simply whether the mask is wide enough to include all animals with non-negligible chance of detection. It seems sigma-hat from your fitted model substantially different to the halfnormal RPSV approximation. Use esa.plot or maybe mask.check to evaluate that evaluate that retrospectively (there may be something useful in secr-habitatmasks.pdf <http://otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-habitatmasks.pdf>).

