You should be able to get this by reading the documentation (recommended), but...
Define a 2-level 'traps' covariate and use its name in the model. If you already have a capthist object CH and vector x of codes, one per detector, then the covariate dataframe can be added and used with
covariates(traps(CH)) <- data.frame(onoff = x)
fit0 <- secr.fit (CH, model = g0 ~ 1, etc.
fitroad <- secr.fit (CH, model = g0 ~ onoff, etc.
AIC(fit0, fitroad)
predict(fitroad, newdata = data.frame(onoff = levels(factor(x))))
Murray

